            "size": "Large",
            "weight": "Bolder",
            "text": "Voters decide five firearms-related ballot questions tomorrow, and ATF's chief counsel has resigned.",
            "wrap": true,
            "spacing": "Small"
          },
          {
            "type": "TextBlock",
            "text": "ATF announced Friday that Chief Counsel Robert Leider, architect of its 34-rule rollback package, has resigned; The Reload expects most rules to survive but flags the no-visit dealer-sales rule as at risk. Tomorrow: MA Question 9, Arkansas Issue 2, Missouri Amendment 8, Idaho's state-gun question and a Lea County, NM tax.",
            "wrap": true,
            "spacing": "Small"
          },
